PTX CoRW-self+alias+surface
"One thread, y and z aliases of global x. The surface load of z reads 2 from the later surface store to y, and the generic load of y reads 1 from the later generic store to z. Generic with generic and surface with surface are morally strong (same proxy, one location, D48), so the two reads-from edges and program order on each address form a cycle: suld z, st z (same address z), ld y (reads it), sust y (same address y), suld z (reads it). SC per location (8.10.5, as NVIDIA's formal model states it: morally strong communication and program order on one address are acyclic) forbids it: forbidden. Coherence and causality alone do not: causality relates operations on aliases only through an alias fence."
{
x=0;
y @ generic aliases x;
z @ generic aliases x;
P0:r0=0;
P0:r1=0;
}
 P0@cta 0,gpu 0       ;
 suld.weak r0, z     ;
 ld.weak r1, y       ;
 st.weak z, 1        ;
 sust.weak y, 2      ;
exists
(P0:r0 == 2 /\ P0:r1 == 1)
